Shared leaderboards face the same problem at community scale. The MS MARCO organizers (Craswell, Mitra, Yilmaz, Campos and Lin, SIGIR 2021) describe their defenses:

- each group may submit at most two runs per month, and at most one that differs only by small changes such as hyperparameters or seeds;
- every submission is public, so p-hacking patterns are visible;
- each run also ranks extra hidden queries that never count on the public board. For the document leaderboard they used 45 TREC 2020 queries as a **private leaderboard**.
